<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CEZ says low demand cuts net outlook.</title>
<headline>Czech CEZ says low demand cuts net outlook.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The main Czech power utility, CEZ a.s., said on Tuesday that lower demand for electricity in a slowing economy would lead to 1997 net profit totalling up to one billion crowns below the company's previous estimate of 6.1 billion crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;In any case (net profit) will go lower than the (previous) prediction by hundreds of millions up to one billion crowns,&quot; Petr Voboril, director of financial planning for CEZ, told Reuters.</p>
</text>
